// SWARM RABBIT HOLE — Wave 13 (Impl-R): Rule R1 (quiescent capture)
// — the non-quiescent case (W2B §4.3: "capture legal only if every
// fallback merge into c is HB-before the capture or after J(W);
// otherwise c enters by contrib/messages only. Without R1:
// conditional determinism"). The static slice-1 rule keeps ONLY the
// provable arm — a fallback merge program-order-BEFORE the wave —
// because "after J(W)" is unprovable by lexical order alone (a
// textually-later merge can still sit BETWEEN two J(W)s when the
// wave is in a loop: the exact conditional-determinism window).
// Mixed use — a merge after the wave on a seam cell — is therefore
// a checked compile error. MUST FAIL TO COMPILE.

ptr c = lcell_new(1)

fn main() {
    wave {
        contrib(c, 1, 0)
    }

    // The mixed-use merge: not HB-before the capture, and not
    // provably after J(W) (loop-shaped capture would reintroduce
    // the window). E-R1 fires HERE, at the merge.
    ptr late = lcell_new(1)
    lcell_inflate(late, 5, 0)
    lcell_merge(c, late)

    print("unreachable")
}
